        "created_at": "2019-04-04T23:54:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So hey RPG players and source book readers, I am curious about something.</p>\n<p>When Christopher says \"the core RPG rule book has a story about X,\" what does that mean exactly?</p>\n<p>Like, is it a few-page short story with descriptions and dialogue between characters and all that? For the GM to read for flavor and setting?</p>\n<p>Or is it more like a set of narrative bullet points for the GM, and then the onus is on the GM to make sure the characters go through the story being told (or roll with it as the characters go off and do something else)?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:39.910Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
