        "id": 226326,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-04-09T02:25:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It was in the question about robotics in the science in multiverse episode. They were talking about different types of robots and how advanced they are, and the fallout in society of the Omnitron event, and Christopher said something like, \"And there's a story about this in the core rulebook.\"</p>\n<p>So I guess my question is, when there's \"a story\" in an RPG sourcebook like this, does the book actually define and tell the story? (And in how much detail?) Or does the story come out kind of however it comes out in each RPG group depending on what the players and GM did, prompted by a couple bullet points from the source book?</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:00:13.067Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
